(D3) partial sharing: 1/N*(rho) = (sqrt(1+rho)-1)/(sqrt(1+rho)+1)  (identity check) and its direction under acceleration of the shared or private part
  rho =    0.1  1/N* = 0.02382  (s-1)/(s+1) = 0.02382
  rho =    0.5  1/N* = 0.10102  (s-1)/(s+1) = 0.10102
  rho =    1.0  1/N* = 0.17157  (s-1)/(s+1) = 0.17157
  rho =    4.0  1/N* = 0.38197  (s-1)/(s+1) = 0.38197
  rho =  100.0  1/N* = 0.81900  (s-1)/(s+1) = 0.81900
  1/N*(rho) increases with rho, so acceleration of the SHARED drift (rho up) widens the range of d/c where pooling wins, and of the PRIVATE drift narrows it.
